433	     *
434	     * The panel has no readable ID register, so "the init sequence was sent"
435	     * has never been evidence that it worked; something has to be drawn at
436	     * boot or a dead panel looks exactly like a working one.
437	     *
438	     * Both panels are revealed together, one stroke segment per step, so the
439	     * word is written left to right.  The step count is the whole cost: the
440	     * panel takes no partial update, so every step pushes a full 51200-byte
441	     * frame to each panel at ~25ms, and the stroke rendering adds to that.
442	     * 20 steps measured 1677ms and was by itself most of the delay between
443	     * reset and a readable screen; 8 steps measured 408ms on the same board
444	     * and still reads as writing rather than appearing.  Keep it at 8 unless
